L#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"Cluster manifests stay on `:local` with `imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent`. After the first successful publish, set the GHCR packages **public** so nodes can pull without `imagePullSecrets`. Rebuild a single image with `workflow_dispatch` (`image=<id>` or `all`)."},"140":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-138","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"Never commit real `ansible/inventory/hosts.ini` (it is gitignored)."},"141":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-139","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"Kubeconfig, tokens, and SSH material are excluded."},"142":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-140","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"The BATS tests mock external commands (including kubectl) so they never touch real clusters or credentials."},"143":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-141","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"Bazel runfiles + explicit data dependencies make exactly what is needed visible (no accidental leakage of host files)."},"144":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-142","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"`MODULE.bazel.lock` is committed (standard for reproducible Bzlmod) and contains only public registry metadata."},"145":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-143","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"See the root `.gitignore` and `.bazelignore` for the full exclusion list."},"146":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-144","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"The following are modeled with first-class Bazel targets:"},"147":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-145","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"`//:manage` as `sh_binary` (`//:manage`)"},"148":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-146","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Full hermetic BATS suite (vendored bats-core)"},"149":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-147","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Kubernetes manifests and overlays as `filegroup` data"},"150":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-148","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Documentation site (`//docs:serve`, `//docs:docs`, `//docs-site:*`)"},"151":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-149","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Includes `//docs:test_generate_shell_docs`, the docs gates in `//:test-fast`, and the export +\n**real browser screenshots vs goldens** in the docs job (visual diffs fail the job and require\nexplicit approval via `//docs-site:visual-linux -- --update` + PR review)."},"152":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-150","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Ansible validation + convenient playbook launchers (`//ansible:*`)"},"153":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-151","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Dashboard dev / build / test wrappers (`//dashboard:*`)"},"154":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-152","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Contributor environment check (`//:doctor`)"},"155":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-153","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Comprehensive root aliases and test suites"},"156":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-154","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Repo-wide ownership gate: `//tests:bazel_file_coverage` proves every tracked file is named by a\nBazel rule, and that each wildcard `glob()` carries a written reason in `SANCTIONED_GLOBS`.\n`bazelisk build //:everything` is the artifact that gate protects; `//:verify` is the gate set."},"157":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-155","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Runtime operations against real hardware (full Ansible playbooks with real inventories, heavy cluster workloads) intentionally remain outside pure Bazel \"build\" semantics and are launched through the `sh_binary` wrappers (`//:manage`, `//ansible:*`)."},"158":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-156","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#using-bazel-for-daily-work","content":"Bazel is the established entry point for every build, test, lint, docs, and operations command. The\nMakefile stays as a compatibility shim for people and jobs without `bazelisk`, and it delegates to\nBazel whenever `bazelisk` is on `PATH`. The few places that still call a script directly (the\ndevcontainer's `postStartCommand` bootstrap, the CI dependency warm-up, `scripts/ci_check_only.sh`)\nare listed with their reasons in project-conventions.md."},"159":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-157","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"First-class multi-arch contributor environment (`.devcontainer/`): **linux/amd64 + linux/arm64**."},"160":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-158","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Host"},"161":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-159","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Notes"},"162":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-160","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"macOS Apple Silicon / Intel"},"163":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-161","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Docker Desktop"},"164":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-162","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Windows x86\\_64"},"165":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-163","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Docker Desktop + WSL2"},"166":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-164","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Linux amd64/arm64"},"167":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-165","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Docker Engine / Podman"},"168":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-166","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"NVIDIA DGX Spark (Grace arm64)"},"169":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-167","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Docker/Podman on-box"},"170":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-168","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Pinned tools (see `.devcontainer/tool-versions.env`, shared with CI): bazelisk, buildifier, shfmt, shellcheck, kubeconform, kubectl, helm, ansible, ruff, mypy, Node **22**, Python **3.11**, prettier, bats, kcov, Grok Build CLI."},"171":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-169","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Full onboarding: **dev-environment.md**."},"172":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-170","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#using-the-dev-container","content":"Open the repo in VS Code or Cursor (