gy\\_check\nValidate the topology and, when kubectl + cluster access exist, compare the\ndeclared nodes against live K3s nodes (read-only drift report)."},"6088":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-932","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#typed-value-contracts","content":"Bash has no type system, so the closest equivalent is validating the *kind* of\nevery value at the boundary where it enters a function: a port that must be an\ninteger in 1..65535, a memory floor that must be a Kubernetes quantity, a tier\nthat must be one of a closed set. Without it, `--memory 24Gig` travels through\nhalf a script before `kubectl` rejects it, or worse, silently means something\nelse."},"6089":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-933","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#typed-value-contracts","content":"Every checker follows one contract:"},"6090":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-934","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#typed-value-contracts","content":"returns 0 when the value satisfies the contract;"},"6091":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-935","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#typed-value-contracts","content":"returns 1 otherwise, having written one diagnostic to **stderr** naming the\nparameter, so stdout stays reserved for data.\nThey never exit the shell, so a sourced library cannot kill its caller; under\n`set -e` a failed check aborts an entry script, which is the intent."},"6092":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-936","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#typed-value-contracts","content":"Libraries here deliberately omit `set -euo pipefail` and inherit the caller's,\nas every other `scripts/lib/*.sh` does (see docs/project-conventions.md §6)."},"6093":{"id":"/generated/shell/