hell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#utility-runner-bazel-entry","content":"Dispatches to `scripts/utilities/<name>.sh` for dashboard-controllable utilities."},"6381":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1225","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#command-run-utility","content":"!!! warning"},"6382":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1226","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Manage GPU graphics clocks on DGX Spark (Blackwell GB10) for thermal stability."},"6383":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1227","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"**Intent**: GB10 has no user-controllable power limit or fan curve on DGX Spark\n(`nvidia-smi -pl` and fan speed return N/A). The only operator-accessible actuator\nis graphics clock locking via `nvidia-smi -lgc`. Range lock (default 300–2200 MHz)\ncaps peak clocks to avoid sustained 78–88°C temps and thermal shutdowns during\nlong-running inference, with near-zero impact on memory-bound MoE workloads."},"6384":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1228","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"**Idempotency** (core of the utility pattern):"},"6385":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1229","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"`status` reports configured lock range, telemetry, and health classification."},"6386":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1230","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"`run` is a no-op when the configured lock range already matches targets."},"6387":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1231","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Service install is idempotent (only rewrites unit if content differs)."},"6388":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1232","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"**Lock readback**: NVML only offers setters for locked GPU clocks\n(`nvmlDeviceSetGpuLockedClocks`), so `nvidia-smi` cannot confirm a `-lgc` request.\nLive `clocks.min/max.graphics` are used whenever the driver reports them; otherwise\nthe range applied during the current boot is read from `SPARK_CLOCK_STATE_FILE`\n(default `/var/lib/spark-clock/lock`). `status` names which source it used."},"6389":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1233","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"**Safety**:"},"6390":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1234","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Never touches ai-inference namespace workloads."},"6391":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1235","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Requires nvidia-smi; mutation verbs require root (or passwordless sudo)."},"6392":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1236","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Respects the lab's GPU Operator + nvidia-persistenced."},"6393":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1237","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Detects PD-degraded states (513–650 MHz / \\~15W) and advises power-cycle."},"6394":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1238","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","cont