 The engine is `scripts/lib/py/lab_topology.py`\n(shell wrapper: `scripts/lib/topology.sh`). `bazelisk run //:manage -- setup` and\n`bazelisk run //:manage -- topology` drive it."],[1333,"The five MiaAI lanes (DeepSeek-V4-Flash DSpark pair, GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 TensorFold pair, Qwen3.8-27B EXL3, Qwen3.8-27B TensorFold, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next TensorFold) refuse Mode A, B, and C **and** each other: one exclusive lane at a time. The two pair lanes use the **2-node pair** NCCL block (`enp1s0f0np0,enp1s0f1np1` / `mlx5_0,mlx5_1`), not the ring block above. The DSpark lane sizes memory with `GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION_TEXT=0.835` only - never hand-set `--gpu-memory-utilization`. The TensorFold lanes are not vLLM, so no vLLM util flag applies to them. Full profiles, images, and upstream recipes: Models catalog."],[4768,"The five supported configurations"],[146,"The following are modeled with first-class Bazel targets:"],[11295,"The four keys every utility's `status` contract promises are validated; the\nrest of the document is utility-specific (see each script's `# @command`\nheader) and passes through untouched, which is what the index signature on\n`UtilityStatus` already records. `z.unknown()` is the honest type for \"whatever\nthis particular utility prints\", and nothing renders those keys generically."],[11187,"The full inference/visual workload status payload."],[1354,"The full stack (`mcp-agent-toolkit-full`) uses `nemotron-retriever-embed` for document chunk embeddings and Qdrant for retrieval — the same RAG pillar as Nemotron and Qwen agentic presets."],[6310,"The gated drowzeys Keys house-qsa abliteration overlay is optional and only fetched\nwhen HF\\_TOKEN is exported and the overlay's terms were accepted (lane default ABLIT\noff). Its exact HF repo id is not confirmed upstream, so override ABLIT\\_REPO once you\nhave the accepted repo id. The whole repo is downloaded at the pinned revision; there\nis no --include filter, so budget the full 96 GiB."],[6190,"The gated refusal-direction ablit (drowzeys/keys-DeepSeekV4Flash-Vision-EXP-ablit) is\noptional and only fetched when HF\\_TOKEN is exported and the repo terms were accepted.\nThe lane ships ABLITERATED=0; the ablit direction is an 18 KiB runtime add-on, not a\nsecond checkpoint."],[51,"The generated trees are ordinary content to the site: `//docs-site:*` targets depend on\n`//docs:content`, which globs `docs/generated/**` alongside the hand-written pages, so a\nregenerated reference invalidates the build and the sidebar picks the new headings up with no\nextra wiring."],[235,"The generator lives in `docs/generate_shell_docs.py`. It is intentionally kept simple (stdlib only) but is being improved for even nicer output formatting."],[42,"The generator now produces:"],[2714,"the generators whose output the site ships"],[3003,"The golden rule and why heavy workloads are dangerous around power events"],[1078,"The host `hermes-lab` stack is a **persistent lab operator*&#x2A;. Coder and Kasm workspaces use a separate &#x2A;*`workspace-dev`** profile for coding assistance:"],[608,"The image starts Hermes `workspace-dev` in the background on session launch. Desktop shortcuts open the dashboard (`:9119`) and Hermes CLI."],[3184,"The instrument and the enforcing gate for each language: TypeScript, Python, Shell, BATS, data files"],[1945,"The lab portal **Agent Chat** panel shows prerequisites, deploy/stop controls, and launch links."],[3114,"The lab uses **production-grade Traefik v3** (official Helm chart) as the unified HTTPS entry point, with **Authelia** for user management and forward-auth SSO. K3s bundled Traefik stays disabled; the standalone Helm install supports CRD middleware chains, TLS, and metrics."],[3249,"the library carries no `set -euo pipefail`, because it inherits the caller's options;"],[11180,"The lifecycle state an inference Job can report. Derived, never re-listed."],[69,"The MkDocs site published two aliases with **mike**; Fumadocs has no mike equivalent, so the\nsame URLs are produced by building the static export twice with different `basePath` values:"],[4898,"The model"],[4861,"The model is TP=1 (many Nemotron nano/super, Qwen3.6 dual, MedGemma)"],[11208,"The monitoring stack status payload."],[1031,"The multi-arch **devcontainer** can install the Hermes **CLI** (`hermes`) for\nlocal agent-assisted coding — see dev-environment.md.\nThat is separate from this page’s **host Docker gateway** on DGX Spark nodes.\nNever commit API keys or `hermes/data/.env` from either path."],[2230,"The multi-arch `.devcontainer/` image (linux/amd64 + arm64) includes bazelisk, buildifier, shfmt, ruff, mypy, ansible, kubectl, helm, kubeconform, shellcheck, bats, yamllint, Node.js 22, Python 3.11, Playwright, and a pinned Grok Build CLI. Versions and checksums are pinned in `.devcontainer/tool-versions.env` (shared with CI). Independent fetch stages keep rebuilds local to the pin that changed. Works on Apple Silicon, Windows (Docker Desktop + WSL2), Linux, and DGX Spark. See dev-environment.md."],[1334,"The Nemotron 3.5 Transcribe 30B-A4B NVFP4 ASR **Deployment** (`family: speech`, 1 GPU, port 8000) has no `manage.sh` verb, like `nemotron-speech-asr` / `nemotron-speech-tts`. Start it from the dashboard or with `bazelisk run //scripts:run-utility -- inference-workloads start nemotron-3.5-transcribe-30b-a4b-nvfp4 --confirm yes` after `download-nemotron-transcribe run`."],[11222,"The Nemotron catalog payload: models, pillars, presets, and optional tiers."],[11251,"The Nemotron stack status payload."],[1797,"The Next.js control plane includes an **Observability** section (`#observability`):"],[709,"The NVIDIA GPU Operator works well on K3s but:"],[3061,"The old 64Gi policy floor reserved \\~192 GiB across three Sparks before any Job, so Mode A (\\~189 GiB) always failed and operators clicked through. That made the guard a paper tiger."],[2808,"The only cluster-operations entry point"],[11273,"The Open WebUI catalog payload."],[11280,"The Open WebUI